 4268 A:ddb9                                    ;
 4269 A:ddb9                                    ; MOST FUNCTIONS TAKE A SINGLE ARGUMENT.
 4270 A:ddb9                                    ; THE RETURN ADDRESS OF THESE FUNCTIONS IS "CHKNUM"
 4271 A:ddb9                                    ; WHICH ASCERTAINS THAT [VALTYP]=0  (NUMERIC).
 4272 A:ddb9                                    ; NORMAL FUNCTIONS THAT RETURN STRING RESULTS
 4273 A:ddb9                                    ; (E.G., CHR$) MUST POP OFF THAT RETURN ADDR AND
 4274 A:ddb9                                    ; RETURN DIRECTLY TO "FRMEVL".
 4275 A:ddb9                                    ;
 4276 A:ddb9                                    ; THE SO-CALLED "FUNNY" FUNCTIONS CAN TAKE MORE THAN ONE ARGUMENT,
 4277 A:ddb9                                    ; THE FIRST OF WHICH MUST BE STRING AND THE SECOND OF WHICH
 4278 A:ddb9                                    ; MUST BE A NUMBER BETWEEN 0 AND 255.
 4279 A:ddb9                                    ; THE CLOSED PARENTHESIS MUST BE CHECKED AND RETURN IS DIRECTLY
 4280 A:ddb9                                    ; TO "FRMEVL" WITH THE TEXT PNTR POINTING BEYOND THE ")".
 4281 A:ddb9                                    ; THE POINTER TO THE DESCRIPTOR OF THE STRING ARGUMENT
